## Installing Asciidoc

Some books I have written have been with _Asciidoc_, mainly
for its ease of creating PDFs and websites with a table of contents.

- <https://ninjas.cl/books/elixir-fullstack/>

- <https://ninjas.cl/books/wren-libro/>

So it is important to have a proper _Asciidoc_ mode.

Since _Doom Emacs_ does not come with this mode preloaded, we are going to install it.

For this we go to the `adoc-mode` project.

```github
bbatsov/adoc-mode | Un major mode de Emacs para editar Asciidoc
```

For this we install with the following set of commands

```text
  M-x package-install RET adoc-mode RET
```

A curious fact is that this mode went a long time without a maintainer, but in 2023
it was revived. A great success and I am grateful to the _Emacs_ community.

- <https://metaredux.com/posts/2023/03/12/adoc-mode-reborn.html>

## Multiple Cursors

Well, this is a feature that was popularized by [Sublime Text](https://forum.sublimetext.com/t/history-of-simultaneous-multi-caret-editing/43253/6).

It consists of being able to select a word and, with a key combination
like `M-d`, other similar ones get selected, allowing the words
to be edited at the same time.

There are some implementations available.

```github
magnars/multiple-cursors.el | Editar en muchos lugares a la vez con Emacs
```

```github
hlissner/evil-multiedit | Edición múltiple para el modo evil de Emacs
```

```github
gabesoft/evil-mc | Múltiples cursores para evil en Emacs
```

_Doom Emacs_ comes with `evil-multiedit` and `evil-mc` integrated.
You just have to enable them in the configuration.

For this we go to the _Doom Emacs_ config.

```text
  SPC f p RET
  init.el
```

Near line 63 we uncomment _multiple-cursors_.

```clojure
multiple-cursors  ; editing in many places at once
```

We save and now we synchronize.

```bash
doom sync
```

Finally we open _Emacs_ again and we will have multiple cursors enabled.

```youtube
zXdT5jY_ui0
```

```youtube
jNa3axo40qM
```

```youtube
Y4cJxdhlxvw
```

There are some people who say this feature is not necessary
because _Emacs_ already ships tools like macros and text replacement.

```youtube
3O-bDYqhFos
```

Personally I believe having multiple cursors helps the transition
from other editors like _Sublime Text_, _VSCode_, or _WebStorm_.

To select the text you can use

```text
C-v
```

And then apply

```text
M-d
```

to select the words to edit.

## Meditations

So far I feel quite excited about learning _Emacs_.
Each time I understand its flow better.

Although it is a bit hard at first to adapt to the new ways of doing things.

It is exciting to feel you learn something new every day, and with an editor
that is more than 40 years old, it seems like a super bet to me.

However it is frustrating in some aspects; I feel extremely
slow compared to other editors and I run into roadblocks
along the way quite often.

But I suppose they are just initial cramps
from not having known _Emacs_ before.

Will I have to unlearn everything I learned in other editors?

- Commands
- Opening files
- Creating projects

It is likewise something that takes time to learn.
